ng back up  obviously there's a difficult balance  between public health and allowing  businesses to survive  do you think our local our national  leaders are striking that balance  properly  well first of all thank you so much for  having me and hopefully i can come back  in  in a better time but this is i mean you  know yes  first of all restaurants is the word  restaurant means to restore your  community  right and um there are 11 million people  working in independent restaurants in  america  and 3 million of them are unemployed  right now  there's also 5 million people more there  are  butchers fishermen other people that  provide services for restaurant right so  that's basically the size of  holland or you know that's a lot of  people that are now  working in the independent restaurant  industry and when  uh congress looks at it they look at  restaurant in terms of  fast casual fast food chain restaurant  those are  very separate businesses some of them  can actually do even better during the  pandemic  there's nothing to do with independent  mom and pop  small businesses so first for us was  very  important to explain on narrative  explain a situation  for the politician because most of them  actually don't understand  what's the difference between a chain  restaurant and a mom and pop  independent restaurant and that's a very  important part  once we explain that this is not a  restaurant issue  this is an american issue that millions  of americans are now without jobs  and we need not more loans we actually  need  long-term solutions grants that  can be forgiven because the restaurant  industry  has on a good day you have 10 profit  margins that means that 90 cents to each  dollar  um goes back into the business that's on  a good day  let's say even five percent and in times  like this  so all the good years that you had you  have to save up for times like this that  it's a it's a new territory right most  restaurants are month to month  and does not have 